{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1194339-how-groups-of-mage-actually-work","id":1194339,"title":"How groups of mage actually work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-11T13:10:15-07:00","id":1194339,"title":"How groups of mage actually work?","content":"I don't really know Mage's lore as much as I'd like to.<br /> <br /> Right know I'm acquiring some sourcebooks before the DriveThru GM's sale ends, and I'd like to know if there's any book on how &quot;groups of mages&quot; (chapels?) work. I mean, how can a disparate group of 4-6 mages work together, when they can have different paradigms, techniques and interests? <br /> <br /> Is there any book on the issue? Please guys, answer before the GM's sale ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:24:24-07:00","id":1194342,"title":"","content":"Doing the same thing myself. Guide to the Traditions has a lot in it, including a table explaining the different levels of Cabal/Chantry/Council.<br /> <br /> Guide to the Technocracy does the same for the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:31:22-07:00","id":1194345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1194339-how-groups-of-mage-actually-work#post1194339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, how can a disparate group of 4-6 mages work together, when they can have different paradigms, techniques and interests?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same way any group of mismatched people work together in a group: by acting like mature adults, and just doing it.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, it's a struggle for mages, working with people who have completely different, utterly contrary worldviews and practices than you. As far as you believe, every other mage group - if not every other mage - is Doing It Wrong.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, mages do it. They have to, when it comes to the Ascension War. Or even just dealing with &quot;normal&quot; everyday mage matters, like vampire incursions or the local church group trying to get your witch coven shut down.<br /> <br /> It's about learning to keep calm, find common ground, not start fights where they aren't needed, and maybe even learn to like those other weirdos who comprise the only Awakened allies hanging out in your neck of the woods. In short, it's a human interaction problem, rather than a strict Focus problem.<br /> <br /> Or here's another answer to your question: With Great Difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T14:53:13-07:00","id":1194372,"title":"","content":"Cabals form from Mages with similar interests or agendas (political activity, waging the Ascension War, research and investigation, being related to each other/ in the same Tradition, preserving Bygones, being in a band together, etc.) as a sort of mutual support group mixed with resistance cell. <br /> <br /> The trick I've found is that before starting any new game/chronicle, get everyone together to talk about the parts of the setting they find interesting, what aspects of it they'd like to explore and the sort of things they'd like to do. Once the interests aspect is covered, issues of paradigm tend to turn into instances of character building/development, sort of like Spock and McCoy arguing over logic vs emotion in Star Trek, at least in my experience. But I find it helps to think of the Cabal (and even the Chantry) as a character in and of itself, one that the entire group has input in the creation and development of. Start with a concept that everyone can agree on, and build from there with their own individual character concepts. <br /> <br /> A long while ago, I was part of a game with a cabal entirely oriented around making money and accruing financial power in order to undermine Technocracy influence. In addition to my radical libertarian free market Virtual Adept, we had an Akashic business woman fixated on the application of Confucian ethics to business and finance, a Verbena &quot;witch of Wall Street&quot; who played the stock market based on Tarot readings, and a member of the Ngoma who was one of South Africa's nouveau riche &quot;black diamonds&quot; trying to find a suitable middle ground between the modern post-Apartheid world and his traditional values and beliefs. Half the game sessions ended up including in-character debates/arguments about the nature and purpose of money and economics in society. It was ... weird. But fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T20:16:23-07:00","id":1194426,"title":"","content":"Shared backgrounds as Library make a big difference. If one mage has a few books on say voodoo and another has a few books on alchemy, they can work together on certain topics.<br /> <br /> Obviously, mages need to find a way to work their paradigms together.<br /> <br /> A good example from my current game: the Order of Hermes washout (long story short, the player wanted an Orphan and went with some GM suggestions after taking the Diabolic Mentor flaw) had to watch a potential mage at a small private college. The OOH washout was given a cover identity as a student, and enrolled in courses. The Virtual Adept in the chantry created a backstopped identity and the player said his character would be a physics and engineering major, since his character is a disciple in Matter (rank 2) and Forces (rank 3). The Virtual Adept assigned the character an advanced physics class, which I decided was Advanced Particle Physics.<br /> <br /> The main project for the class is to build a working laser and the player's OOH washout character with one dot of Science and the player's lack of real-world physics education (me, too, but I have a B.A. in Biology and took Physics in high school so I can at least fake some understanding), the OOH washout asked the chantry for help building the project.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adept is pretty good in physics, given his work in forces and with computers, but his paradigm is Everything is Data, which is pretty different than the paradigm of the OOH washout's paradigm, A World of Gods and Monsters. To the Virtual Adept, everything works because it is logical and data and you just have to code. That means he saw physics in a very technological way and the OOH washout has elementalism as one of his practices, barely knows about the occult and has little in ritual (his main power manifestation is martial arts--character could have easily been an Akashic Brother). So, the Virtual Adept's explanation of how to make a laser was less than scintillating. The two Hermetics in the chantry both know forces, but their paradigms aren't perfect fits. The House Quaesitor member is a labor lawyer and believes in Divine Order and Earthly Chaos, essentially that God made things perfect and that human moral failings make the world messed up. A World of Gods and Monsters assumes that the universe is hostile in general and that things have powers because they do-mages are just another type of monster. The Quaesitor is not a scientist, so he really doesn't get how you build a laser for college.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for the OOH washout PC, the chantry leader is an Order of Hermes mage of House Ex Miscellena who teaches college-level Environmental Science and has the Techgnosi Merit. The chantry leader blends technology and mysticism, seeing technology only as codified ritual magick the consensus has accepted. With a paradigm of Unlocking the Keys to Reality, the chantry leader sees the entire universe as God's creation, which humans are meant to use their reason and faith to discover. So, a laser works because you believe it works, but there are better ways to make a laser work because certain rules of physics have been accepted. So, the chantry leader, who has rank 4 in Forces with a specialty in Life and rank 4 in science, could easily say, 'well we'd call it this in the Order of Hermes, but it works like this if you follow this rule set. Oh, and here's the math to build that laser.' The OOH washout PC has 2 dots in Academics, so he can do enough math to make the laser work for class. With Forces 3 and Prime 2, he could just make a laser, but since he needs a college paper explaining it, now he has the language needed to do so. Thus, even if he takes a laser-building shortcut, it can be 'coincidental' because he has the right words to say.<br /> <br /> TLDR version: mages work together with a lot of effort. They have to find common ground to work magick together and teach each other. However, joining a group gives you lots of power guarding your back. As for systems, chantry-building is not a strength of rules made for Mage as of this writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:24:32-07:00","id":1195388,"title":"","content":"Thank all you guys for the answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T12:41:56-07:00","id":1196877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1194339-how-groups-of-mage-actually-work#post1194339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really know Mage's lore as much as I'd like to.<br /> <br /> Right know I'm acquiring some sourcebooks before the DriveThru GM's sale ends, and I'd like to know if there's any book on how &quot;groups of mages&quot; (chapels?) work. I mean, how can a disparate group of 4-6 mages work together, when they can have different paradigms, techniques and interests?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of very incompatible Paradigms, world views and interests, some Mages in a Cabal might view other Mages in the Cabal principally as possible converts to their outlook(s) and methods in the future ; and if this doesn't happen or if it can't happen, then they might view them as aware or unaware allies to their cause.<br /> If one or both of these possibilities happen, then Magickal interactions and choices in regards to Magick in the Cabal might be influenced and be dependant on these attitudes and events that occur (at least partly) due to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-18-2018, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T15:46:01-07:00","id":1196929,"title":"","content":"I remember my old ST being asked the same question. He was describing the various traditions to our soon-to-be gaming group, when he was stopped and asked:<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, So, how do you keep all these differing factions going towards the same goal?&quot;<br /> <br /> His response: &quot;Oh...some cosmological horror usually does the trick&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}